  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo></math> be a sequence such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math>. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>28</mn><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;are the first&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;prime numbers, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to</p>",
